ïµ>␀®Ã␀À7É␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ƒ+@␀␀E ␀␀␀␀␀␀ß␀␀␀?2HBß?bß?à?ß?NElite␀ÿ␀	Info␀°		Keys␀Ö	CreditsG␀␀␀␀The gameW␀␀The screen.␀␀LeavingU␀␀FlyingÎ␀␀Weaponsn␀␀Jumps␀␀ScreensD␀␀Chartså␀␀Freeze␀␀SavingÅ␀␀Elite	v␀␀This version
5␀ELITEThe ZX Spectrum Elite for the expanded Z88: the original Z80game code runs here, with its graphics and text redrawn for theZ88 screen.The MENU topics have the keys.␀The game, the screen, and leaving it.␀The Spectrum keys, as in the original. LEFT SHIFT is theSpectrum's CAPS SHIFT and RIGHT SHIFT its SYMBOL SHIFT.␀Who wrote what.␀You start docked at Lave with a Cobra Mk III, 100 credits and apulse laser. Trade between systems, fight pirates and police,buy better equipment, and work your way up from Harmless toElite across eight galaxies.␀The map on the right holds the 3D view and the scanner, or achart. On the left are the instruments (fuel, shields,temperatures, speed, roll and dive, energy banks, missiles,compass), the view's name and the flight messages. Text screenssuch as Status and Market Prices fill the whole width.␀INDEX suspends the game and it carries on where you left it.ESC does not quit; to end the game, KILL it from the Index.␀S and X climb and dive, N and M roll. SPACE speeds up and RIGHTSHIFT slows down. 1, 2, 3 and 4 show the front, rear, left andright views. Docked, 1 launches.␀A (or 0) fires the laser. T targets a missile, F fires it and Uunarms it. E sets off the ECM, W the energy bomb, Q launchesthe escape pod and C switches on the docking computer: eachonly once fitted.TAB brings an enemy in at once (added for this version, forpractice).␀Pick a system on a chart, then press H in flight: the countdownstarts and the jump follows if you have the fuel. With agalactic hyperdrive fitted, G and H together take you to thenext galaxy.␀I galactic chart, O short-range chart, P data on the system, Kmarket prices, L status, ENTER inventory. Docked: 2 buys cargo,3 sells cargo, 4 equips the ship.␀N, M, S and X move the cursor, B puts it back on your system, Dgives the distance to the nearest system and R finds a systemby name. On the short-range chart each system has a number; thenames are listed on the left, the one under the cursorhighlighted and a * after those within jump range.␀LEFT SHIFT freezes the game. Then SPACE carries on and 1 startsa new game. S turns the sound on and Q turns it off. B, D, R, Yand K set the Spectrum's joystick and keyboard options.␀Docked, RIGHT SHIFT opens the commander menu: 1 loads, 2 saves,3 goes back. A commander is saved as a file named after him,with .elt added (JAMESON.elt for the default name).␀Elite by Ian Bell and David Braben (1984). The ZX Spectrumversion by Torus, published by Firebird in 1985. This card runsthat version's Z80 code, taken from the elite-skoolkitdisassembly.␀The Z88 front end draws the 3D view, scanner, charts andinstruments natively, puts all text in OZ windows, reads thekeyboard directly in flight, and plays the effects on the Z88'sspeaker. The Lenslok check is gone. Needs an expanded Z88 with48K of free RAM.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀